<title>UK: NIB sets 150 billion lire 10-year bond.</title>
<headline>NIB sets 150 billion lire 10-year bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond was announced by lead manager Cariplo S.P.A and Chase Manhatten.</p>
<p> BORROWER   NORDIC INVESTMENT BANK</p>
<p> AMT    150 BLN ITL   COUPON    *8.0	 MATURITY  **07.MAR.07</p>
<p> TYPE  FIX/REV FRN    ISS PRICE  100.90    PAY DATE    07.MAR.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  2.00	REOFFER    99.00     LISTING     LONDON</p>
<p> NOTES     *FOR YEARS ONE TO FIVE THEN 12.75 PCT MINUS THE</p>
<p>		REFERENCE RATE 12M LIBOR, FIXING ANNUALLY SUBJECT TO</p>
<p>		A MINIMUM COUPON OF 3.5 PCT</p>
<p>	    **CALL OPTION ON 07.MAR.02.</p>
<p> MOODY/S&amp;P  =	   DENOMS (M) 5-50	SALE LIMITS US/UK/IT</p>
<p> NEG PLG    NO	  CRS DEFLT  NO	  FORCE MAJ   IPMA 2</p>
<p> GOV LAW    ENGLISH   HOME CTRY  =	   TAX PROVS   STANDARD</p>
<p> MGT/UND    0.375     SELL CONC  1.625     PRAECIPUUM  =</p>
<p> NOTES	ISSUED OFF AN EMTN PROGRAMME (AAA/AAA)</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
